    "title": "Expose typed pqueue index query API",
    "description": "Update pqueue's query surface so callers query typed ESF indexes without raw Vec\u003cVec\u003cu8\u003e\u003e escape hatches. Keep pqueue name-based query identity from QueueIndex.name. In-scope files: crates/pqueue/src/lib.rs, crates/pqueue-engine/src/port.rs, crates/pqueue-projection/src/lib.rs, tests. Add typed query methods accepting serde_json::Value values or a small typed key wrapper; deprecate or internally adapt old raw byte query methods only for legacy indexes if necessary. Ensure unique/non-unique query APIs use axon_esf encoding and validate arity/type errors. Out-of-scope: SQL implementation for relational backends.",
